{
  "rationale": "Use a minimal plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the deterministic exploration policy in one specification automaton with small helper recovery/commit states. The policy prefers random_walk in clear exploration, inserts short forward pulses for progress, uses obstacle-specific directed turns, uses brief backward escape only for front blockage, and returns to exploration quickly when path_clear is observed. Action states self-loop on path_clear so intended one-shot commands are not preempted, while obstacle events can still force safe recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion using two simple plant automata",
    "Encode the full deterministic policy in a single specification with exactly one controllable enabled per non-terminal policy state",
    "Use random_walk as the default clear-state action and alternate with a short move_forward state for steady coverage",
    "Route obstacle_front to a dedicated backward recovery, obstacle_left to clockwise turn recovery, and obstacle_right to counterclockwise turn recovery",
    "Keep recovery conservative and one-shot, then return to exploration immediately when path_clear is available"
  ],
